# UI standards

Portfolio-grade B2B SaaS: clear hierarchy, cards, subtle borders, readable tables, status badges, consistent spacing. Not tutorial CRUD. Dark mode via `next-themes` if the shell already supports it.

Prefer Server Components. Validate with Zod + React Hook Form. Do not hardcode business rules in the UI — hide/disable actions, still enforce on the server.

## Every list/detail page

Must render **loading** (skeleton), **empty**, **error**, and **success**. No blank screens.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
if (!rows.length) return null

// ✅ GOOD
if (error) return <ErrorState title="Could not load leads" onRetry={refetch} />
if (!rows.length) return (
  <EmptyState
    title="No leads yet"
    description="Capture a lead to start the sales pipeline."
    action={{ label: "Create lead", href: "/leads/new" }}
  />
)
```

## Reuse before creating

`DataTable`, `SearchInput`, `FilterBar`, `Pagination`, `StatusBadge`, `EmptyState`, `ErrorState`, `ConfirmDialog`, `FormField`, `MoneyDisplay`, `DateDisplay`, `Avatar`, `UserSelect`, `ProjectStatusBadge`, `BidStatusBadge`.

If a primitive is missing, add it under `components/` once, then use it.

## Patterns

- Sidebar groups: Dashboard, CRM, Delivery, Finance, Reports, Notifications, Settings.
- Tables: sortable columns, server pagination, row click → detail. Destructive actions use `ConfirmDialog` + toast.
- Money always through `MoneyDisplay` (org currency). Status always through a badge, not raw enums.
- Client portal and freelancer portal use the same primitives but **different field sets** (see business-rules).
- Layout must work on phone, tablet, and desktop: hamburger + sheet nav below `lg`, no horizontal page scroll, `min-w-0` on flex children, 44px tap targets, `text-base` inputs on mobile (iOS zoom), safe-area padding.
